# Line-ending policy. Everything checks out as LF on every platform, so a
# Windows clone cannot rewrite text files to CRLF. This repository depends on
# exact bytes more than most: the bit-exactness gate compares two encodes with
# `cmp`, conformance vectors are pinned by hash, and the frozen specification
# assets are normative literals. A CRLF rewrite breaks those comparisons for a
# reason that is slow to diagnose.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Streams and raw video are byte-exact fixtures. Never normalize them.
*.kfv binary
*.y4m binary

# Binary — never convert
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
